  "truthSource": "manual_audit",
  "truthReference": "Independent hand audit of validation/m12/fixtures/swift/*.swift against Swift semantics and the Systems-family contract (Java M12.02 / C# M12.07 / ObjC M12.19 / Rust M12.18). Symbols: protocol -> interface with methods -> method and associatedtype -> type; class -> class with properties -> property and methods -> method; open class visibility open; init -> constructor named \"constructor\" (Java/C# naming); struct -> struct with properties -> property; enum -> enum with cases -> enum_member (raw type in metadata only — NEVER an implements edge); extension -> extension symbol named after the EXTENDED type with NO self-owner (members attach to it via contains); actor -> actor; typealias -> type; file-scope functions -> function, type-scope -> method. Noise (negative fixture): function-local let/var -> no symbol, parameters -> no symbol, closures and their params -> no symbol, type references (String/Int/Array/[User]) -> NO uses edges, bare stdlib calls (print, String(...)) filtered, switch `case` patterns -> not enum_member. Relationships (family contract): contains = REAL container ownership only (type/extension -> member); extends = class -> superclass (first inheritance base); implements = class -> adopted protocol (remaining bases); calls = member calls with LEAF target (users.first -> first, users.append -> append, items.map -> map; source = enclosing method); instantiates = bare CAPITALIZED call User(...) -> instantiates ONLY (Swift construction syntax, Java new Foo() analog — never also a calls edge); uses = member reads (self.-rooted AND reads through a local of a declared type), source = the enclosing METHOD per the M49 W15 #814 ruling, target = field leaf (name from self.name, id from u.id); overrides = qualified Owner.method -> Parent.method resolved via the class hierarchy + companion index (UserService.describe -> BaseService.describe); references = file-scope imports (root -> module). AMENDED 2026-09-25 (#933, the swift half): this audit stopped describing the analyzer in two documented ways. (a) Its four `uses` facts were sourced at the enclosing TYPE, but the M49 W15 #814 ruling moved every `uses` source to the enclosing METHOD, so each stale fact read as a false negative while the analyzer's correct twin read as a false positive; the two that were pure source moves are corrected in place. (b) Two facts cited an assignment LHS (`self.name = name`, `self.id = id`) as a 'self. read', which contradicts SCD1 (M37 #599 — a write is never a read) and the lane's own `write-gate` fixture; the analyzer correctly emits nothing for them, so they are DELETED rather than kept as refusal pins (there is no edge to pair with). The audit also never described four genuine member reads (an enum-case read, a `$0.id` element read, a local's property read, and a member read on a String local); every one was read back against the fixture SOURCE TEXT — each fact's evidence reference quotes its line — before being added. The three bare field reads the analyzer emits at confidence 0.6 are pinned as expectedState=unknown. Totals: 80 -> 85 facts (2 deleted, 2 re-sourced, 4 added, 3 refusal pins).",
